      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Vibration needs two physical effects ",
        "bounds": [
          838200,
          365125,
          10515600,
          1325563
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "One effect is called a (viscous) spring. It’s the springiness in many things around you. (I will ignore “viscous”). It has a property we call stiffness.\nThe other effect is called mass. \nWe will now discuss each of these to understand what vibration is, and remmebr how important vibration is: \nIt’s what you feel when you hit a bump in your car\nIt’s music\nIt’s boom and bust in economics\nIt’s oscillation in SGD\nIt’s the motion of the air in your vocal tract and the motion of your vocal folds, when you speak",
        "bounds": [
          838200,
          1825625,
          10515600,
          4351338
        ]
      }
    ],
    "speakerNotes": ""
  },
